      "nets": ["NET0163", "NET0008", "NET0161", "NET0042"],
      "observed": "Both FCC STM32H753 VCAP pins are connected to NET0163 and NET0008, which are routed to the UART3_FCC2 connector. Both NAVC STM32F405 VCAP pins are connected to NET0161 and NET0042, which are routed to peripheral/debug connector signals. No VCAP capacitors to ground are shown.",
      "expected": "The STM32 internal-regulator VCAP pins should have their required capacitors to ground and should not be used as UART, I2C, or other external signal nets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "FCC2 STM32H753VITx: pins 48 and 73 are labelled VCAP and connected to NET0163 and NET0008; FCC sheet, page 2."
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "UART3_FCC2 connector pins 3 and 4 carry NET0163 and NET0008; FCC Peripherals sheet, page 5."
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "NAVC2 STM32F405RGTx: pins 31 and 47 are labelled VCAP_1 and VCAP_2 and connected to NET0161 and NET0042; NAVC sheet, page 3."
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "NET0161 is on the I2C3_NAVC2 connector and NET0042 is routed to the CH330 debug interface; NAVC Peripherals sheet, page 6, and Connections sheet, page 4."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "The FCC is populated with an STM32H753VITx and the NAVC with an STM32F405RGTx."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU internal core regulators may fail to operate correctly or be damaged without the required VCAP capacitors. The VCAP nets also expose the regulator pins to external signal circuitry, potentially preventing reliable MCU operation and disrupting the connected interfaces.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic routes the VCAP pins of both MCUs to external interface signals and shows no required VCAP-to-ground capacitors. This is a significant power-integrity and connectivity error likely to prevent reliable operation of the controllers."
}

